14–2016, children aged 6–17 years whose parent or guardian indicated the child had serious emotional or behavioral difficulties (EBDs) were almost four times as likely to miss >10 days of school because of illness or injury compared with children without serious EBDs (13.4%26#37; compared with 3.5%26#37;). Among children with serious EBDs, those aged 6–10 years were less likely (8.0%26#37;) to miss >10 days of school compared with children aged 11–14 years (15.6%26#37;) and children aged 15–17 years (19.5%26#37;). Among children without serious EBDs those aged 15–17 years (4.7%26#37;) were more likely to miss >10 school days compared with children aged 6–10 years (3.0%26#37;) and children aged 11–14 years (3.3%26#37;).","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":694,"renderedHeight":460,"naturalWidth":694,"naturalHeight":460,"loading":null,"decoding":"async","altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 737 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":25967},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/5.0/img/logo/cdc-logo-tag-right.svg","alt":"Centers for Disease Control and Prevention","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":283,"renderedHeight":66,"naturalWidth":827,"naturalHeight":193,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":4780},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/contrib/libs/cdc/c2r/crlogo.svg","alt":"Content Credentials logo","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":25,"renderedHeight":150,"naturalWidth":150,"naturalHeight":150,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":1490}]},"standards":{"engine":"standards","checks":[{"id":"schema-gov","label":"schema.org GovernmentOrganization markup","pass":false,"detail":